---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import LastVerified from '../../components/LastVerified.astro';
import QuickAnswer from '../../components/QuickAnswer.astro';
import RelatedGuides from '../../components/RelatedGuides.astro';
import SourceList from '../../components/SourceList.astro';
import UpdateBadge from '../../components/UpdateBadge.astro';
import AdsterraNativeBanner from '../../components/AdsterraNativeBanner.astro';
import { latestAppliedPatch, patch107, patch110, patch111 } from '../../data/sources';

const title = 'Is DragonSword Awakening Multiplayer? Co-op Explained';
const description = "DragonSword Awakening co-op covers Subjugation and Raids. See confirmed lobby features and the evidence limits for story co-op, player count and crossplay.";
const canonical = 'https://dragonswordguide.com/multiplayer/';
const reviewedDate = 'October 22, 2026';
const breadcrumb = { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'BreadcrumbList', itemListElement: [{ '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://dragonswordguide.com/' }, { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Multiplayer', item: canonical }] };
const article = { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'Article', headline: title, description, mainEntityOfPage: canonical, datePublished: '2026-08-08', dateModified: '2026-10-22', publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'DragonSword Guide' } };
const sources = [
  { label: 'Official Steam store page', href: 'https://store.steampowered.com/app/4570720/DragonSword__Awakening/', note: 'OFFICIAL_VERIFIED: lists Single-player and Online Co-op.' },
  { label: 'Official Steam update notes 1.0.7', href: patch107.resolvedHref, note: 'Official applied notes: introduced Quick Entry; the search-range setting was later removed in 1.0.11.' },
  { label: 'Official update notes 1.0.11', href: patch111.resolvedHref, note: 'OFFICIAL_VERIFIED: confirms Retry, fastest-response lobby search, version notices, departure notifications and lobby fixes.' },
  { label: 'Official update notes 1.0.10', href: patch110.resolvedHref, note: 'OFFICIAL_VERIFIED: multiplayer lobbies disband the party when the party leader is unresponsive for a long time.' },
  { label: 'Hound13 developer discussion', href: 'https://steamcommunity.com/app/4570720/discussions/0/802344445710375983/', note: 'Developer replies: Subjugation and Raids with friends or random players through Steam lobbies; story co-op was not ready for launch. This is not confirmation of a later story-co-op release.' },
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} routeId="multiplayer" ogType="article" schema={[article, breadcrumb]}>
  <div class="shell page-wrap">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'DragonSword Guide', href: '/' }, { label: 'Multiplayer' }]} />
    <article>
      <header class="article-header">
        <p class="eyebrow">Guide · Co-op scope</p>
        <h1>Is DragonSword Awakening Multiplayer?</h1>
        <LastVerified date={reviewedDate} label="Sources reviewed" />
      </header>

      <QuickAnswer title="Yes — Subjugation and Raids support online co-op.">
        <p>Steam lists Online Co-op. Hound13 identifies Subjugation and Raids as activities you can play with friends or random players through Steam lobbies. Current story and open-world co-op, player count and crossplay are not confirmed by the sources reviewed here.</p>
      </QuickAnswer>

      <div class="article-body">
        <h2>What Can You Play Together?</h2>
        <figure class="scope-figure">
          <img src="/media/multiplayer/co-op-scope.svg" width="600" height="760" alt="Co-op scope: friends or random players connect through Steam lobbies for Subjugation and Raids. Story and open-world co-op, player count and crossplay remain unconfirmed in the reviewed sources." />
          <figcaption>Editorial scope diagram, not a game screenshot or menu sequence. Lines show the developer-described relationship between players, lobbies and activities; they do not specify a party size.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <p><strong>Story and open world:</strong> Hound13 said story co-op was not ready for launch and discussed possible later support. That statement does not establish availability in the current build. Open-world co-op is also unconfirmed in the reviewed sources.</p>
        <p><strong>Solo play:</strong> Steam also lists Single-player. The co-op label does not mean the entire RPG is a shared campaign.</p>

        <h2>Friends, Random Players and Lobby Features</h2>
        <p>The developer describes Steam lobbies as the connection for playing with friends or random players. The patch notes confirm the features below, but do not supply a complete invitation walkthrough.</p>
        <dl class="lobby-features">
          <div><dt>Quick Entry and matching</dt><dd>Update 1.0.7 introduced Quick Entry. Update 1.0.11 removed the old lobby search-range setting; lobbies are searched by fastest response time.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Invite codes and version notices</dt><dd>Update 1.0.11 confirms invite-code joins through a notice shown when the party leader's version differs. Quick Entry also shows a notice when a higher version exists. These notes do not establish the full menu path or a fix for every connection problem.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Retry after a clear or wipe</dt><dd>The party leader can select Retry after a final clear or party wipe to restart a Hunt/Raid, according to Update 1.0.11.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>When the party leader leaves or stops responding</dt><dd>Update 1.0.11 describes a warning that the party may disband if its leader leaves. Update 1.0.10 documents disbanding after a long period of leader inactivity; it does not give an exact timeout.</dd></div>
        </dl>

        <p class="evidence-note"><strong>Before planning a session:</strong> exact player count, unlock level or quest, the full invite/menu sequence, crossplay, cross-save, shared progression, loot ownership and region restrictions remain unverified here. These are evidence gaps, not a claim that each feature is absent.</p>
        <p class="version-context">Game update reference: <UpdateBadge label={`${latestAppliedPatch.label} · ${latestAppliedPatch.date}`} href={latestAppliedPatch.href} /> The badge identifies the latest recorded game patch. The lobby details above cite their own applied notes; the source-review date is not a claim of hands-on testing.</p>

        <AdsterraNativeBanner />

        <h2>Other Multiplayer Questions</h2>
        <details>
          <summary>Is DragonSword: Awakening an MMO?</summary>
          <p>The official description presents a single-player action RPG with selected online co-op activities, rather than a shared-world MMO.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Does it have PvP?</summary>
          <p>No PvP feature was verified in the primary sources reviewed here. The confirmed multiplayer activities discussed above are cooperative PvE.</p>
        </details>
        <p class="next-read">For character setup comparisons, use <a href="/builds/">Builds</a>; for Hero handoffs, use <a href="/teams/">Teams</a>; for status conditions and Signal Skills, use the <a href="/guides/combat-system/">combat guide</a>. Those are separate from the multiplayer scope covered here.</p>
      </div>

      <SourceList sources={sources} intro="The Steam listing, applied patch notes and developer replies support the scope described above. The diagram is our editorial summary; this page does not claim hands-on verification of an invitation sequence or the current game's unconfirmed features." />
      <RelatedGuides links={[{ label: 'Gameplay Systems', href: '/gameplay/' }, { label: 'Hero Handoff Guide', href: '/teams/' }, { label: 'Beginner Guide', href: '/guides/beginner/' }, { label: 'Roadmap', href: '/roadmap/' }]} />
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-wrap { padding: 1.25rem 0 2rem; }
  .article-header { margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
  .eyebrow { color: var(--accent-light); font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  h1, h2 { line-height: 1.2; letter-spacing: -0.025em; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 7vw, 5rem); margin: 0 0 0.75rem; max-width: 760px; }
  h2 { font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 4vw, 1.75rem); margin: 2.5rem 0 0.8rem; }
  p { margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  .article-body { max-width: 800px; }
  .article-body a { font-weight: 700; }
  .scope-figure { margin: 1rem 0 1.5rem; max-width: 600px; }
  .scope-figure img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: 14px; }
  figcaption { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.85rem; line-height: 1.5; margin-top: 0.75rem; }
  .lobby-features { margin: 1rem 0 1.5rem; }
  .lobby-features div { padding: 1rem 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  dt { font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 0.35rem; }
  dd { margin: 0; color: var(--muted-strong); }
  .evidence-note { padding: 1rem; border-left: 2px solid var(--accent); background: var(--paper); color: var(--muted-strong); }
  .version-context, .next-read { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .next-read { margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  details { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 1rem 0; }
  details:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  summary { cursor: pointer; font-weight: 700; min-height: 44px; padding-top: 0.4rem; }
  details p { margin: 0.65rem 0 0; color: var(--muted); }
</style>
